WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:10.619
If you learned Moon Animator, your hands already know Cadence. Every keybind was kept on purpose.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.840
Press the question mark to see the whole sheet. Numpad and top-row digits both work, exactly like Moon.

3
00:00:18.221 --> 00:00:21.557
Nine opens the add menu. Let's take an R15.

4
00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:29.234
W is move, E is rotate, T is inverse kinematics, and R cycles through the tools.

5
00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:38.761
Select a part, rotate it, and press S to key the pose. Auto-key is already on, so A turns it off if you prefer to key by hand.

6
00:00:39.143 --> 00:00:44.063
The arrow keys step one frame. Hold Shift to step five at a time.

7
00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:46.003
Key a second pose here.

8
00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:53.633
J and K jump between keyframes, Home and End jump to the start and the end.

9
00:00:54.014 --> 00:00:59.054
N turns on onion skin for the selected part, so you can see the frames on either side.

10
00:00:59.435 --> 00:01:02.363
Tab toggles looping, and Space plays.

11
00:01:03.512 --> 00:01:08.192
F frames whatever is selected, and Control Z undoes anything.

12
00:01:09.173 --> 00:01:13.565
Nothing to relearn. Open the sheet with the question mark whenever you need it.

